## Where the code lives

Each term above points at one or two source files. Here they are in one place — what each is, and the
learning-path module that exercises it — so you can jump straight to the part you want to read.

- **`AgentLoop.java`** — the main agent: builds the system prompt and owns the session, then hands the
  loop to `AgentEngine`. Exercised in Module 2.
- **`AgentEngine.java`** — the shared think → act → observe loop (`converse`), used by both the main agent
  and the sub-agent. It enforces the permission modes and fences tool output. Exercised in Module 2;
  traced line by line in `docs/TRACE_EDIT.md`.
- **`ToolRegistry.java`** — the catalogue of tools the model is allowed to call. Add a tool here and the
  model can use it immediately. Exercised in Module 2.
- **`BuiltinTools.java`** — the implementations of the built-in tools (`read_file`, `write_file`,
  `edit_file`, `run_command`, `web_fetch`, and so on). Exercised in Modules 4 and 8.
- **`PermissionService.java`** — decides whether a tool call may run, based on the mode (`ASK`, `AUTO`,
  or `PLAN`). Exercised in Modules 4 and 5.
- **`CheckpointStore.java`** — snapshots a file before it changes and restores it on rewind. Exercised in
  Module 6.
- **`ProjectContext.java`** — loads `IMINI.md` (and `CLAUDE.md` / `AGENTS.md`) and adds it to the system
  prompt every turn. Exercised in Module 7.
- **`IMINI.example.md`** — the commented template for project memory; copy it to `IMINI.md` to use it.
  Exercised in Module 7.
- **`McpManager.java`** — loads external MCP tool servers from `mcp.json` and exposes their tools.
  Exercised in Module 10.
- **`Untrusted.java`** — wraps web/MCP output in clear fence markers and flags injection attempts.
  Exercised in Module 11.

New here? Read in this order: this glossary, then `ARCHITECTURE.md`, then `docs/TRACE_EDIT.md`, then
`docs/LEARNING_PATH.md` module by module.
